# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# Read this before adding anything: the server runs here now, as the function in
# api/index.py, and that function imports `backend/app` and mounts the shop from
# "Textile Retail Shop". Excluding either of those does not make a smaller
# deployment — it makes one that builds cleanly and then 500s on every request,
# which is a far more expensive mistake than a few uploaded megabytes. That is
# exactly what an earlier version of this file did.
#
# So this lists only things nothing at runtime opens.

# The phone's native shell and its build. The PWA the shell wraps is served by
# the function from backend/app/mobile, which stays.
android/
mobile-app/

# Documentation and screenshots.
docs/
*.md

# Virtualenvs — host-specific, and "Textile Retail Shop/.venv-win" alone is
# 55 MB of vendored packages. Vercel installs from requirements.txt instead.
**/.venv
**/.venv-win
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Local state. The deployment keeps none of this on disk: the database is
# Postgres and uploaded invoices are in Blob storage. A database copied up here
# would be read by nobody and would ship this laptop's data to a public host.
*.db
*.db.bak*
backend/data/uploads/
backend/data/settings.json

.git/
.github/
.env
